# tests/rcu — MIT #22 RCU + lock-free name cache (week 11)

Stub created week 2 (design gate). Cache/RCU API in docs/design.md §2.5.

## Planned tests

- `rc-loop`: N threads hammer `open/stat/close` on a shared directory tree; total
  lookup counter advances, `namestat` hit-rate ≥ 95% after warmup.
- `rc-storm`: concurrent create/unlink/rename storm across N threads while lookups
  run; no use-after-free (debug-poisoned dentries trip an assert), no wrong-inode
  opens (each fd fstat-validated against expected inum).
- `rc-grace`: hold + release read-side sections at max rate; grace_periods counter
  advances; deferred frees complete (freed-entry counter matches).
- `rc-hitrate`: hot-path bench vs stock `namei` (baseline: openclose 16 µs @ CPUS=1);
  speedup recorded in bench/baseline.txt.

## Pass criteria

Storm test passes 3 consecutive runs at CPUS=2 with zero UAF/wrong-inode; hit-rate +
speedup numbers recorded; lite-fallback (locked cache) only per plan risk rule.
